{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#564","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#564","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#564\",\"parent_revision\":\"5d077863a00f685060ca68ad3a6a64de0b5949abffbd524136ab76781a6578a8\",\"root_revision\":\"5d077863a00f685060ca68ad3a6a64de0b5949abffbd524136ab76781a6578a8\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: 2026-04-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\ntest_live_validation.py has 3 tests failing due to GitHub API dependencies and cascading `KeyError: 'item_title'`. Tests need proper mocking or fixture updates to work without live GitHub access.\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nGoal: Fix 3 failing tests in test_live_validation.py so the suite passes in CI without requiring live GitHub API access.\\n\\nDecision: APPROVED\\n\\nConditions:\\n1. Failing tests identity | DERIVABLE \u2014 cascade from missing live_items[\\\"item_title\\\"] when fixture GitHub call fails\\n2. Root cause of KeyError | DERIVABLE \u2014 fixture sets key only on success; no success = no key = all 3 downstream tests fail\\n3. GitHub API injection points | AVAILABLE \u2014 backlog_add, backlog_update, backlog_close MCP tool calls\\n4. Existing mock patterns | DERIVABLE \u2014 test_backlog_core_operations.py covers equivalent operations with mocks\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-03-10T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nGoal: Fix 3 failing tests in test_live_validation.py so the suite passes in CI without requiring live GitHub API access.\\n\\nDecision: APPROVED\\n\\nConditions:\\n1. Failing tests identity | DERIVABLE \u2014 cascade from missing live_items[\\\"item_title\\\"] when fixture GitHub call fails\\n2. Root cause of KeyError | DERIVABLE \u2014 fixture sets key only on success; no success = no key = all 3 downstream tests fail\\n3. GitHub API injection points | AVAILABLE \u2014 backlog_add, backlog_update, backlog_close MCP tool calls\\n4. Existing mock patterns | DERIVABLE \u2014 test_backlog_core_operations.py covers equivalent operations with mocks\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-03-10T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-03-10T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **fix 3 failing tests in test_live_validation.py (github api deps + keyerror)** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: PR #561 code review \u2014 pre-existing issue\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-10\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-03-24)\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\n1. `uv sync` \u2014 install dependencies\\n2. Run without GitHub credentials: `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/tests/test_live_validation.py -v`\\n3. Observe 3 failures \u2014 all in the class reading live_items[\\\"item_title\\\"] \u2014 with KeyError: 'item_title'\\n\\nRoot cause: fixture sets live_items[\\\"item_title\\\"] = result[\\\"title\\\"] only on success; GitHub API failure leaves key absent, cascading to all 3 dependent tests.\\n\\n### Output / Evidence\\n\\nAcceptance Criteria:\\n1. `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/tests/test_live_validation.py -v` exits 0 without GITHUB_TOKEN in CI\\n2. No test raises KeyError: 'item_title'\\n3. test_backlog_core_operations.py suite continues to pass unchanged\\n4. `uv run prek run --files plugins/development-harness/tests/test_live_validation.py` exits 0\\n\\nEffort: Small \u2014 fix fixture setup mock; pattern already exists in test_backlog_core_operations.py\\n\\n### Scope\\n\\nFixture setup for the live validation class calls backlog_add against real GitHub API.\\nFix: mock that call so live_items is populated without network access.\\nPattern exists in test_backlog_core_operations.py.\\nFixing fixture setup resolves all 3 failures (cascade from single root cause).\\n\\n### Prior Work\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-03-10T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Failing tests | plugins/development-harness/tests/test_live_validation.py |\\n| Mock pattern | plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_operations.py |\\n| API surface | plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py |\\n| API surface | plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py |\\n| Agent | @python3-development:python-pytest-architect |\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-03-30T05:11:33Z</sub>\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Failing tests | plugins/development-harness/tests/test_live_validation.py |\\n| Mock pattern | plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_operations.py |\\n| API surface | plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py |\\n| API surface | plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py |\\n| Agent | @python-engineering:python-pytest-architect |\\n</div>\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\nDepends on: None\\nBlocks: Any PR touching backlog_core/ \u2014 those PRs see false CI failures until this is resolved\\n\",\"digest\":\"2496e827f996f518a6289d1efd9b7ffdd9df3d18a5632a383e7c1651571da4cc\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVCuOCw\"}"}